{"ok": false, "issues": ["The exemptions text wrongly lists Section 202, Section 811, and the HUD-mortgage Rent Supplement, Section 8 Loan Management Set Aside and Project-based Section 8 units as exempt. D006 says these units are 'partially covered by the Rent Ordinance regardless of unit type.' D006 also says tenants in fully or partially covered units cannot be evicted without just cause, so these units are subject to this rule. The exemptions field is not in the editable set and should be corrected separately by removing those subsidy categories. The requirement is revised to state their coverage explicitly.", "coverage_conditions says partially covered new construction has a Certificate of Occupancy issued 'after June 1980.' D006 says 'after 1980.' This is not an editable field; flagged for separate review.", "The owner move-in relocation amounts in key_value ($19,413 standard; $6,471 additional; 1.5% CPI-U increase) are not in the provided excerpts and could not be verified. They are left unchanged pending source confirmation.", "status, subject, coverage_logic (null/null), yields_to_local and preempts_local are consistent with the sources. The rule covers all fully and partially covered units, and the remaining exemptions depend on facts outside the allowed fields."], "fix": {"requirement": "Landlords cannot evict tenants in units fully or partially covered by the Rent Ordinance without just cause. This includes partially covered Section 202, Section 811 and HUD-mortgage subsidized units. Measure BB tightened the grounds and notice rules: nonpayment evictions require rental debt of at least one month of HUD Fair Market Rent, refusal to sign a substantially similar lease is no longer a ground, and termination notices, notices to quit and summons/complaints must be filed with the Rent Board within three business days of service."}}
